Theorem TF-12: PartialApply emits NO TF-11 demand (captures via TF-13)

  Preconditions:
    - PartialApply { closure_fn, captures } is the closure-construction
      instruction per Annex E §AIMS TF-7 (forward: FRESH(NonReusable))
    - Per Annex E §AIMS TF-12: "PartialApply emits NO TF-11 demand.
      Captured arg demand handled by TF-13."
    - Captured arguments are NOT subject to the TF-11 standard backward
      demand (which would emit `(arg, Once, Linear)` per capture). The
      captured-arg demand is delegated entirely to TF-13
      `capture_state_update` (proven at TF-13.proof).
    - Rationale (lives at Annex E §AIMS TF-13): captured args propagate
      demand via the LAM-style capture-state-update which couples closure
      cardinality with capture cardinality. A standard TF-11 demand would
      double-count (TF-11 emitting + TF-13 transferring on the same operand)
      AND would not couple closure-cardinality to capture cardinality
      (closure cardinality > Once means each capture is used Many times).

  Soundness property:
    Forall partial_apply in {PartialApply { closure_fn, captures }}.
      backward_demand_tf12(partial_apply) = EMPTY
    AND L-6 monotonicity vacuous (empty demand emission — no codomain state
    to monotone over).

  Proof obligation:
    Two-part discharge:
      (a) Empty-demand confirmation — backward_demand_tf12(PartialApply)
          returns an empty list (no captures, no closure_fn, no captured
          arg appears in the demand output).
      (b) Capture-demand-delegation confirmation — the TF-13 path
          (capture_state_update) is the EXCLUSIVE owner of captured-arg
          demand. No double-counting at TF-12.

    Part (a) — empty-demand confirmation:
      Per Annex E §AIMS TF-12: "PartialApply emits NO TF-11 demand."
      Verified: backward_demand_tf12() returns an empty Vec for the
      PartialApply variant. The closure_fn operand (the function reference
      being partially applied) carries NO TF-11 demand at TF-12 — it is a
      symbolic function handle, not a refcounted value.

    Part (b) — capture-demand-delegation confirmation:
      Per Annex E §AIMS TF-12: "Captured arg demand handled by TF-13."
      Verified: The §3 TF-11 table row for PartialApply does NOT exist
      (PartialApply is omitted from the 14-row table per the §3 TF-11
      statement). The §3 TF-13 statement is the SSOT for captured-arg
      demand. TF-12's contract is precisely "no TF-11 emission" — the
      delegation is a closure of the joint TF-11 + TF-13 specification.
      Negative witness: if TF-12 were to emit `(capture, Once, Linear)`
      via TF-11, the TF-13 capture_state_update would re-process the same
      capture and double-count its demand (Linear + Linear = Unrestricted
      per seq_add — would falsely promote consumption).

    Engines dispatched:
      monotonicity (PRIMARY — vacuous monotonicity for empty backward demand
        per section_04::verify_tf12_partialapply_no_demand)
      case_analysis (PRIMARY — confirm PartialApply absent from §3 TF-11
        table AND backward_demand_tf12 emits empty per
        section_04::verify_tf12_partialapply_no_demand)
      lattice (SECONDARY — accepts gracefully; no codomain element)
      refinement (SECONDARY — accepts gracefully; TF-12 emits no refine())

  Expected:
    status: valid
    reason: section_04 monotonicity + case_analysis engines discharge TF-12 via empty-demand confirmation + TF-11-table-absence verification + TF-13 capture-demand-delegation chain-of-custody
